     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Less effective and more expensive than oral therapy, but an alternative first-line option for superficial or early distal lateral subungual disease (few adverse effects or interactions)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Once daily for 24 weeks (fingernails) or 48 weeks (toenails). Complete cure rates: efinaconazole 10% 15.2 to 17.8%, tavaborole 5% 6.5 to 9.1%, ciclopirox 8% 5.5 to 8.5% (at 48 weeks)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Efinaconazole and tavaborole penetrate the nail plate and beat older topicals; topical treatment works especially well in children (thinner, faster-growing nails)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Adverse effects are mostly at the application site: exfoliation, erythema, burning, dermatitis"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
